Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 battle report background fills the gutters

The post-battle report (exp, level-up, items won) draws a scrolling pattern
that repeats every 96 pixels, like the field menu. It was the one screen shown
after every 16:9 battle that stayed 4:3, so the picture narrowed to a
pillarbox between the battle and the field. With widescreen on, the
background is drawn twice more, 96 pixels to each side, so it covers the
gutters at every scroll; the port's gutter policy (port/options/widescreen.c)
gives the report overlay the menu gutter. The panels, header and footer keep
their 4:3 positions in the middle. Off, nothing changes.

--- a/src/battle/report/report.c	2026-10-23 15:00:00.000000000 -0300
+++ b/src/battle/report/report.c	2026-10-23 15:00:00.000000000 -0300
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include "battle/report.h"
 #if PORT_HOST
 #include <stdio.h>
+#include "port_widescreen.h"
 #endif
 
 /* Creates the report's text windows: the exp, its label and the two-line
@@ -46,6 +47,14 @@
         report->bgSkip = 1;
     }
     sprite.draw(FILE_CACHE.getEntry((FILE_FGTREP_SPRITES - 1) << 16), 0x1E, report->bgScroll, report->bgScroll);
+#if PORT_HOST
+    /* Widescreen: the pattern repeats every 96 pixels; two more copies
+       cover the side gutters at every scroll */
+    if (dw3_port_widescreen_px() > 0) {
+        sprite.draw(FILE_CACHE.getEntry((FILE_FGTREP_SPRITES - 1) << 16), 0x1E, report->bgScroll - 96, report->bgScroll);
+        sprite.draw(FILE_CACHE.getEntry((FILE_FGTREP_SPRITES - 1) << 16), 0x1E, report->bgScroll + 96, report->bgScroll);
+    }
+#endif
     sprite.setLayerId(report->layer, report->depth - 1);
     if (report->header.level != 0) {
         if (report->header.level != 0x1000) {
